    "Live notes" : {},
    "Loading OpenRouter's model list..." : {},
    "Loading…" : {},
    "Lower means more literal. WhisperShortcut uses 0.0, which reproduces what was said. Sending no value at all — as versions before 7.96 did — leaves the AI model on its own setting of 1.0, the most likely source of invented or swapped words." : {},
    "macOS blocked WhisperShortcut from reading system-prompts.md (%@). Until that is fixed, the app uses its default prompts. Your file has not been changed. Give WhisperShortcut Full Disk Access in Privacy & Security, then quit and reopen the app." : {},
    "macOS permissions" : {},
    "Make changes directly" : {},
    "Manage usage" : {},
    "Measured so far" : {},
    "Microphone is off in System Settings. You can continue and enable it later." : {},
    "Model tag served locally (e.g. an Ollama tag). Pull it first: `ollama pull <model>`. Prefer a plain instruct model — reasoning models spend their first seconds thinking before any text appears. Default: %@" : {},
    "Model:" : {},
    "More models" : {},
    "More models, %lld" : {},
    "More thinking can help on hard audio, accents, and unusual vocabulary, at the cost of latency — on Flash-Lite the cost is close to zero, on Pro it roughly doubles. Gemini 3.1 Pro and Gemini 3.7 Flash cannot run below Low and are clamped to it." : {},
    "Moved %@ to the Trash." : {},
    "Needed for Screen Recording or Accessibility changes to take effect." : {},
    "Needs \"Save usage data\" in Smart Improvement. Then you can ask \"why did it get that wrong?\" and the AI app looks at your recent dictations." : {},
    "New access key…" : {},
    "New Command…" : {},
    "New in this version: WhisperShortcut can tell me how often each feature is used and whether it worked. Counts only, like “12 dictations, 1 failed”. Never your words, audio, or which apps you use. No ID, no tracking." : {},
    "New to OpenRouter? The same flow creates the account. You pay OpenRouter directly for what you use." : {},
